WEBVTT

00:00:18.900 --> 00:00:21.110
Cheers, once again.

00:00:21.110 --> 00:00:23.770
Welcome to our mountain lab.

00:00:25.620 --> 00:00:26.470
Thanks.

00:00:32.480 --> 00:00:35.370
So, now that you've been 
assigned to this place,

00:00:35.370 --> 00:00:39.070
there's a certain secret we 
need to let you in on.

00:00:39.070 --> 00:00:41.750
A... secret?

00:00:42.290 --> 00:00:43.270
Yeah...

00:00:45.050 --> 00:00:49.840
A secret that you can't 
reveal to anyone.

00:00:52.570 --> 00:00:57.080
Abilities of distinguished individuals, 
numerous throughout history,

00:00:57.080 --> 00:00:59.370
have been stored in special E-genes.

00:00:58.450 --> 00:00:59.370
<b>E-genes</b>

00:00:59.800 --> 00:01:02.960
The E-gene holders, 
who inherit those genes,

00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:04.710
<b>AU balls</b>

00:01:03.460 --> 00:01:08.750
summon the abilities sleeping 
within them via AU balls,

00:01:08.750 --> 00:01:11.280
and embody AU weapons.

00:01:12.630 --> 00:01:18.120
The E-gene holders belonging to the 
supranational organization Dogoo

00:01:18.120 --> 00:01:21.120
versus enemies from outer space 
known as Evolutionary Invasion Objects.

00:01:21.120 --> 00:01:24.470
This is the chronicle of their 
fateful battle for humanity!

00:02:58.400 --> 00:03:01.170
Gun No. 6: Monster Meat

00:03:08.040 --> 00:03:09.710
<i>Tiger</i> to <i>Alex Logan</i>.

00:03:10.510 --> 00:03:12.750
We're currently passing over Alaska.

00:03:13.560 --> 00:03:15.570
This is <i>Alex Logan</i>.

00:03:15.570 --> 00:03:18.690
What is the status of the Invasion Object 
specimen you collected?

00:03:18.690 --> 00:03:23.780
No issues. There was actually no need 
to have the First Platoon come along.

00:03:23.780 --> 00:03:25.950
Heh, roger that. Get back safely!

00:03:27.280 --> 00:03:29.500
It's snowing harder now...

00:03:30.570 --> 00:03:31.550
A new recruit?

00:03:31.980 --> 00:03:35.070
Yeah, in the Second Platoon, I heard.

00:03:35.650 --> 00:03:39.290
With a sniping weapon. 
Codename, if I remember, is...

00:03:40.500 --> 00:03:41.800
Nobunagun.

00:03:42.540 --> 00:03:45.480
I heard about that. 
A Japanese girl, right?

00:03:46.580 --> 00:03:47.870
Oh, that's great news—

00:03:48.440 --> 00:03:50.730
for the wimps in the 
Second Platoon, too.

00:03:51.080 --> 00:03:54.710
Maybe now they'll be 
more on our level.

00:03:55.180 --> 00:03:58.650
But, Princess, that new recruit 
is unfortunately

00:03:58.650 --> 00:04:01.220
utterly useless as a sniper.

00:04:01.220 --> 00:04:05.520
Oh, boy. So just a big pain in 
Jack the Ripper's neck, then.

00:04:06.310 --> 00:04:07.820
Actually, about that...

00:04:07.820 --> 00:04:13.720
She fought an amazing aerial battle with Jack,
 and shot an armored Object dead—

00:04:14.160 --> 00:04:16.520
It sounds like she's doing a 
bang-up job over there.

00:04:17.030 --> 00:04:21.730
Wow, you seem to know 
all about her, Gaudi.

00:04:21.730 --> 00:04:24.780
Got the hots for the new recruit?

00:04:25.820 --> 00:04:28.110
N-No, that's not it at all, Cyx!

00:04:28.800 --> 00:04:31.910
It's about ten years too early for you 
to be worrying about girls.

00:04:35.540 --> 00:04:38.050
L-Leave me alone!

00:04:43.980 --> 00:04:45.060
What's going on?!

00:04:45.060 --> 00:04:47.170
We're experiencing some turbulence 
due to the wind and snow.

00:04:49.960 --> 00:04:52.280
Can't see a thing in this white-out.

00:04:58.050 --> 00:04:59.680
Princess, what should we do?

00:04:59.770 --> 00:05:01.160
What <i>can</i> we do?

00:05:01.980 --> 00:05:05.320
Just as long as we don't die 
here with that thing!

00:05:07.460 --> 00:05:09.080
It's no good. At this rate—

00:05:09.220 --> 00:05:13.750
Gaudi, c'mon! Use your weapon 
and do something!

00:05:14.040 --> 00:05:16.410
Sure, "something," but what?!

00:05:17.200 --> 00:05:18.260
Got it!

00:05:56.410 --> 00:05:58.150
We made it!

00:06:06.610 --> 00:06:07.810
The container's undamaged!

00:06:08.310 --> 00:06:10.020
Any contact from H.Q.?

00:06:10.020 --> 00:06:11.590
No. We can't get through.

00:06:12.210 --> 00:06:14.530
It'll probably be impossible until 
this blizzard slows down.

00:06:16.390 --> 00:06:18.130
Geronimo, are you oka—?

00:06:19.940 --> 00:06:24.110
Did you forget how much the 
princess hates the cold?

00:06:24.190 --> 00:06:25.740
Ah, right...

00:06:26.510 --> 00:06:31.470
It appears there's a civilian research 
facility 3 km up this mountain.

00:06:33.100 --> 00:06:36.620
If they have communications equipment, 
we can get in touch with H.Q.

00:06:37.160 --> 00:06:38.870
Okay, I'll go—!

00:06:40.320 --> 00:06:42.710
We'll be back after we contact H.Q.!

00:06:42.710 --> 00:06:44.480
You keep an eye on the container!

00:06:44.480 --> 00:06:47.340
Aww, that's so mean!

00:06:47.340 --> 00:06:49.630
Going off without me 
to somewhere warm!

00:07:05.780 --> 00:07:06.760
Princess?

00:07:07.450 --> 00:07:09.030
Ah, I'm fine.

00:07:12.530 --> 00:07:16.700
It seems we have a visitor 
despite this blizzard.

00:07:17.660 --> 00:07:22.290
I see. Let us show them a most 
courteous welcome...

00:07:27.660 --> 00:07:29.320
It's awfully quiet in here.

00:07:31.680 --> 00:07:33.980
There's no way they'd be out...

00:07:35.500 --> 00:07:37.260
Can I help you?

00:07:39.180 --> 00:07:41.370
Our plane made an emergency landing 
at the foot of the mountain.

00:07:42.510 --> 00:07:44.440
How distressing.

00:07:44.440 --> 00:07:46.240
Could we borrow your radio?

00:07:47.290 --> 00:07:48.400
Of course.

00:07:49.900 --> 00:07:53.770
Excuse me for asking, but to which 
armed forces do you belong?

00:07:54.250 --> 00:07:55.410
We're Dogoo.

00:07:55.410 --> 00:07:56.240
Princess!

00:07:57.770 --> 00:07:59.140
Dogoo...

00:08:05.280 --> 00:08:08.100
Sorry, but we're keeping 
our friends waiting.

00:08:08.580 --> 00:08:10.680
We don't really have time to 
sit down to a leisurely meal.

00:08:10.680 --> 00:08:12.600
Don't mind if I do!

00:08:13.670 --> 00:08:14.910
Princess...

00:08:17.420 --> 00:08:20.350
By the way... uh...

00:08:20.350 --> 00:08:22.450
My name is Gonda.

00:08:22.450 --> 00:08:24.850
Gonda, you're here alone?

00:08:25.460 --> 00:08:26.240
Yes.

00:08:26.240 --> 00:08:28.430
You're up this far in the 
mountains alone?!

00:08:28.430 --> 00:08:32.140
Well, these days pretty much 
every lab is cutting costs...

00:08:33.030 --> 00:08:38.050
More importantly, if you're Dogoo, 
you must be fighting those monsters, huh?

00:08:38.050 --> 00:08:39.540
Monsters?

00:08:39.540 --> 00:08:41.890
He means the Evolutionary 
Invasion Objects.

00:08:41.890 --> 00:08:42.810
That's right!

00:08:44.720 --> 00:08:48.200
Evolutionary... Invasion Objects.

00:08:50.530 --> 00:08:53.530
You said you made an emergency landing...

00:08:54.120 --> 00:08:56.830
Could it be that a monster—

00:08:58.120 --> 00:09:03.050
no, an "Evolutionary Invasion Object"— 
is aboard your plane?

00:09:09.750 --> 00:09:11.910
That's an industrial secret.

00:09:11.910 --> 00:09:14.210
More of a military secret.

00:09:18.720 --> 00:09:20.690
I was surprised as well.

00:09:21.400 --> 00:09:24.480
No, it seems they haven't realized yet.

00:09:32.190 --> 00:09:33.700
Crud, we can't get through.

00:09:34.620 --> 00:09:39.870
Well, it's just this blizzard. 
The temperature outside is -30.

00:09:39.870 --> 00:09:42.730
A human'll freeze solid in just a few hours.

00:09:42.730 --> 00:09:45.450
That's nothing to smirk about.

00:09:45.450 --> 00:09:47.700
You're right. That was 
inappropriate of me.

00:09:48.130 --> 00:09:52.430
The princess doesn't like to be cold, and she 
doesn't like to talk about being cold, either.

00:09:53.200 --> 00:09:55.700
Well, this blizzard should 
slow down by morning.

00:09:56.640 --> 00:10:00.490
I've love to have your companions over 
and hear all about the monster—

00:10:00.490 --> 00:10:05.300
err, the
Evolutionary Invasion Object.

00:10:09.490 --> 00:10:11.170
So warrrrrm.

00:10:11.170 --> 00:10:15.510
Jeez, Japanese people really are 
crazy about monsters, huh?

00:10:16.410 --> 00:10:18.080
But what should we do, Princess?

00:10:18.600 --> 00:10:23.140
It seems like we don't have a choice but 
to wait out the blizzard, as he says.

00:10:23.550 --> 00:10:26.240
Should we call Gaudi and the rest, 
and spend the ni—

00:10:26.240 --> 00:10:29.780
Even if the blizzard stops, 
we can't use the radio.

00:10:31.130 --> 00:10:32.390
What do you mean?

00:10:32.800 --> 00:10:36.500
That radio... is totally busted.

00:10:36.500 --> 00:10:37.390
What?

00:10:37.790 --> 00:10:39.090
Or rather...

00:10:41.300 --> 00:10:43.150
...someone totally busted it.

00:10:44.130 --> 00:10:46.630
Wait a minute, what are you saying?

00:10:51.490 --> 00:10:54.750
Are those... blood stains?!

00:10:55.270 --> 00:10:57.280
There's definitely one here.

00:10:57.280 --> 00:10:59.170
"One"? One what?!

00:11:01.740 --> 00:11:02.900
A monster...

00:11:10.210 --> 00:11:12.350
No matter how you look at it, 
this is messed up.

00:11:12.350 --> 00:11:16.920
I've never heard of an Evolutionary Invasion 
Object appearing on a snowy mountain!

00:11:16.920 --> 00:11:18.350
That's for sure!

00:11:19.170 --> 00:11:21.680
But, I saw it in his eyes...

00:11:42.930 --> 00:11:44.030
That guy!

00:11:56.410 --> 00:11:57.410
Princess!

00:12:25.700 --> 00:12:27.020
Those were...

00:12:27.820 --> 00:12:29.850
...E-gene holders...

00:12:30.150 --> 00:12:31.400
You bastard!

00:12:31.400 --> 00:12:32.440
No!

00:12:32.440 --> 00:12:33.010
Princess!

00:12:33.480 --> 00:12:36.110
We mustn't turn our powers on a human.

00:12:36.110 --> 00:12:38.920
But, Princess, he tried to kill you!

00:12:38.920 --> 00:12:40.550
Even so, I won't allow it!

00:12:45.990 --> 00:12:48.470
Where is he going? Is he running away?

00:12:57.280 --> 00:12:58.260
It turned on!

00:13:03.560 --> 00:13:04.800
He—!

00:13:05.650 --> 00:13:08.280
I see. They're...

00:13:08.950 --> 00:13:11.770
...E-gene holders!

00:13:41.130 --> 00:13:43.360
You met Nobunagun?!

00:13:43.830 --> 00:13:47.520
Yeah, before we went to 
pick you guys up.

00:13:47.520 --> 00:13:49.410
On <i>Alex Logan</i>.

00:13:49.410 --> 00:13:51.240
She was pretty cute, too.

00:13:51.730 --> 00:13:53.190
Really?!

00:13:54.520 --> 00:13:58.410
Well, not like I'm super 
interested or anything.

00:13:58.410 --> 00:14:00.070
Wanna see a pic?

00:14:00.070 --> 00:14:01.270
I would.

00:14:01.270 --> 00:14:02.430
You have one?!

00:14:06.690 --> 00:14:10.870
In a s-s-s-swimsuit?!

00:14:10.870 --> 00:14:12.050
You can have it.

00:14:12.050 --> 00:14:13.390
Are you sure?

00:14:13.390 --> 00:14:15.360
We can always ask Capa for more.

00:14:15.360 --> 00:14:16.720
Thank you so much!

00:14:19.330 --> 00:14:22.520
She's so cute, and that 
body is something else!

00:14:23.860 --> 00:14:28.400
The Second Platoon must be... awesome.

00:14:28.860 --> 00:14:31.070
You must have it pretty rough.

00:14:31.070 --> 00:14:34.780
Getting bawled out day after day 
by such a scary lady.

00:14:34.780 --> 00:14:37.530
Huh? Whadaya mean by that?!

00:14:37.530 --> 00:14:42.090
I'm not even a tiny bit 
scared of her.

00:14:43.860 --> 00:14:45.440
C-Cyx's back!

00:14:53.030 --> 00:14:54.270
...A snowmobile?

00:14:56.070 --> 00:14:57.560
That's not Cyx and the 
princess at all!

00:15:08.580 --> 00:15:09.600
Run!

00:15:20.110 --> 00:15:21.040
Princess!

00:15:21.330 --> 00:15:23.580
Just as I thought. We gotta hurry!

00:15:31.070 --> 00:15:36.440
E-E-Everyone else is... dead.

00:15:37.500 --> 00:15:39.020
He was... no good.

00:15:40.020 --> 00:15:43.800
He... He's gone completely insane!

00:15:45.880 --> 00:15:51.140
He... He's convinced that... 
that a monster—

00:15:51.140 --> 00:15:54.340
that an Evolutionary Invasion Object 
is living inside him!

00:15:55.810 --> 00:15:58.460
The secret is, as follows...

00:15:58.460 --> 00:16:01.350
At this lab in the snowy mountains,

00:16:01.350 --> 00:16:05.590
the only thing we have to look forward 
to is mealtime. Don't you think?

00:16:06.550 --> 00:16:07.610
Sure...

00:16:08.060 --> 00:16:10.600
So sometimes we secretly,
 under the table,

00:16:10.600 --> 00:16:14.360
procure something you don't 
normally get to eat.

00:16:15.590 --> 00:16:19.000
Something... you don't 
normally get to eat?

00:16:19.740 --> 00:16:23.540
That's right! The meat you ate earlier...

00:16:23.540 --> 00:16:25.500
What kind of meat do you think it was?

00:16:25.960 --> 00:16:28.610
It was a special meat, you know.

00:16:30.780 --> 00:16:32.670
It was monster meat!

00:16:33.930 --> 00:16:38.860
You've seen 'em on TV, right? Those things 
they call "Evolutionary Invasion Objects."

00:16:58.870 --> 00:17:02.310
The snowmobile... Why?

00:17:11.420 --> 00:17:12.510
Smells like...

00:17:13.360 --> 00:17:14.070
...explosives!

00:17:21.510 --> 00:17:23.350
Just as I thought!

00:17:23.350 --> 00:17:27.870
You <i>are</i> transporting an 
Evolutionary Invasion Object!

00:17:31.100 --> 00:17:33.530
Who are you?

00:17:41.280 --> 00:17:45.010
Watch out! Run! There's an 
Invasion Object in there!

00:17:45.920 --> 00:17:50.150
Run? Why would I have to 
run from a friend?

00:17:55.300 --> 00:17:59.510
Listen up. I'm not gonna be 
caught by the likes of Dogoo.

00:18:00.980 --> 00:18:02.080
I...

00:18:03.810 --> 00:18:05.040
...can't forgive you guys!

00:18:06.100 --> 00:18:07.300
You... {TB: In Japanese the verb is omitted here which we can't do so I made the explanation of why he can't forgive them more natural in English.}

00:18:08.300 --> 00:18:11.000
...killed...

00:18:11.080 --> 00:18:13.090
...my friends!

00:18:15.840 --> 00:18:20.560
Of course it was a lie that 
it was monster meat!

00:18:20.560 --> 00:18:25.620
We just wanted to pull his leg a bit.

00:18:25.620 --> 00:18:29.760
But then... he took us seriously...

00:18:31.900 --> 00:18:32.880
Gaudi!

00:18:36.710 --> 00:18:37.810
Geronimo...

00:18:49.970 --> 00:18:51.340
Gaudi, stop that thing!

00:18:53.190 --> 00:18:53.710
R-Right!

00:18:58.610 --> 00:18:59.530
Attack!

00:18:59.690 --> 00:19:00.510
Roger!

00:19:07.140 --> 00:19:08.840
We can't get anywhere 
near it like this!

00:19:09.870 --> 00:19:11.900
I guess we'll have to take it out.

00:19:13.600 --> 00:19:14.570
Let's fly!

00:19:14.570 --> 00:19:15.380
Got it!

00:19:15.380 --> 00:19:16.230
Okay!

00:20:02.880 --> 00:20:05.830
Gonda has breathed his last.

00:20:06.960 --> 00:20:08.040
I see.

00:20:09.580 --> 00:20:11.920
To think that an Invasion Object 
is living inside you...

00:20:13.400 --> 00:20:17.690
To be convinced something 
like that is true...!

00:20:18.290 --> 00:20:20.810
But how could he have known?

00:20:20.810 --> 00:20:23.580
So high up in the mountains 
in this snow...

00:20:23.580 --> 00:20:26.070
To him, these conditions were extreme.

00:20:26.770 --> 00:20:28.150
Still, though!

00:20:28.660 --> 00:20:30.650
There's no telling how 
we'd fare, either.

00:20:31.810 --> 00:20:36.870
We don't know what would happen if we 
were pushed to extremes like that.

00:21:02.390 --> 00:21:05.440
Oh, here it is. Phew!

00:21:05.440 --> 00:21:07.280
What are you up to, anyway?

00:21:07.280 --> 00:21:09.750
N-Nothing at all.

00:21:10.100 --> 00:21:11.920
Maybe you were looking for something?

00:21:11.920 --> 00:21:14.310
Well, yes, you could say that.

00:21:16.080 --> 00:21:17.530
A swimsuit shot?

00:21:17.530 --> 00:21:21.100
That's min— my friend's! {TB: Literally "That's not mine," but it's funny because the "not" in Japanese comes at the end and it's obvious he stuck it there as an afterthought so I tweaked it to get the joke in.}

00:21:21.100 --> 00:21:23.400
Oh? Well, I'll toss it, then.

00:21:26.600 --> 00:21:29.600
Please don't throw it away!

00:21:30.120 --> 00:21:32.750
It's actually mine!

00:21:39.900 --> 00:21:42.090
I'm sorry I lied...

00:21:42.090 --> 00:21:44.090
Such a good, honest boy.

00:23:25.490 --> 00:23:27.130
Time for <i>Cooking with Galiko</i>!

00:23:27.130 --> 00:23:30.820
The important thing is the sauce. 
The secret ingredient is a healthy one: vinegar!

00:23:30.820 --> 00:23:32.520
How is it, Mr. Vidocq?

00:23:32.520 --> 00:23:33.660
Awful!

00:23:33.660 --> 00:23:35.160
Oh no!

00:23:35.160 --> 00:23:37.840
Next time, Gun No. 7, "Musashi Wonder"!

00:23:37.840 --> 00:23:39.870
I'll do better next time!
